00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.440
Now for a quick grammar bite.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.900
In Russian, Adjective must match the gender of the noun.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.060
Хлеб вкусный, uses the masculine ending.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.420
Вода вкусная, uses the feminine ending.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.200
Яблоко вкусное, uses the neuter ending.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.340
English keeps the adjective the same no matter what.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:51.120
Russian adds E, I, or O, so the words agree.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.980
Now you can describe your food correctly,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.580
want to know a secret about one of today's words.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.920
The Russian word Chai and the English word T are cousins.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.560
Bots started as Chai in China.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.400
The word traveled along ancient trade routes

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.100
and reached Russian in the 1600s.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.800
English took a different path,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.940
through Dutch and Portuguese traders.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.300
Be careful, though.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.320
The word магазine sounds like магазine,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.340
but means shop.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.260
Next time you see Pt,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.060
remember it shares the same route as Chai.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.400
In Russia, bread is treated with great respect.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.140
Famili soft and share one big loaf at the table.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:34.480
Children are early, that throwing away bread is considered unlucky.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.480
A traditional welcome gift is a loaf of bread with salt.

